; walk-t0x-slide — the tempo slides once per NON-row tick.
;
; `T02` on row 0 walks the tempo down two per tick for the five ticks of
; the row that are not tick 0; `T12` on row 1 walks it back up. Every
; step is its own tempo segment, and the tempo comes home — only the
; channel memories tell the second pass from the first.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
